      "documentation": {
        "documentation": {
          "title": {
            "canonicalEnglish": "Run and manage CPN-based workflow factories"
          },
          "description": {
            "canonicalEnglish": "Run and manage CPN-based workflow factories.\n\nWhat:\nCPN-based workflow factory CLI for running factories, submitting work, and inspecting live sessions.\n\nHow to use:\nRun you run --work ./docs/examples/startup-work.json to start the current Factory with explicit Work and the local dashboard (http://localhost:7437/dashboard/ui).\nUse you run --dir factory --work ./docs/examples/startup-work.json for an explicit Factory directory. See you \u003ccmd\u003e --help for subcommand details.\n\nAgents:\nStart with you docs agents for orientation, you submit or you submit batch to enqueue work, and you session list to confirm a live factory.\nRun you docs for all packaged reference topics. Use --verbose or --debug for stderr diagnostics; full policy in you docs."
          }
        },
        "examples": [
          "you run --work ./docs/examples/startup-work.json",
          "you docs agents"
        ]
      },
      "visibility": "visible",
      "runnable": true,
      "usage": {
        "line": "you",
        "example": "  # Start the default Codex-backed Factory with explicit Work.\n  you run --work ./docs/examples/startup-work.json\n\n  # Agent orientation and command matrix.\n  you docs agents"
      },
